      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"System failure\" is a conservative term, but a basic translation script is a recipe for intermittent, hard-to-trace errors that will cost you far more time than the middleware. The middleware isn't just a best practice; it's the robust abstraction layer that handles connection pooling, error retries, and schema drift—all things a quick script simply cannot manage reliably. If you push this without proper abstraction, you won't just miss the Q3 window; you'll be in a week-long debugging nightmare trying to fix data integrity issues.",
      "source": "target",
